<title>USA: Freddie Mac to redeem $39 mln in debentures.</title>
<headline>Freddie Mac to redeem $39 mln in debentures.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freddie Mac said Wednesday that on June 5 it will redeem the entire principal amount of two fixed-rate debenture issues totaling $39 million as follows.</p>
<p> Principal   Interest  Maturity    Cusip</p>
<p>  $25 million	8.04    05/19/06  3134A0J78</p>
<p>  $14 million	6.50    09/25/98  3134A1BT6</p>
<p>Freddie Mac said payment of 100 percent of principal plus interest accrued to the redemption date will be made to holders on record as of the close of business June 4.</p>
<p>Freddie Mac is a corporation chartered by Congress that buys mortgages from lenders and packages them into securities for investors.</p>
</text>
